lejepa_norm.data.corruptions
============================

`functions.py` is derived from the `imagecorruptions` package, version 1.1.2
(https://github.com/bethgelab/imagecorruptions, Apache License 2.0), by
Evgenia Rusak and Benjamin Mitzkus (Bethge Lab). That package is itself a
pip-installable port of the corruption code released with

  Dan Hendrycks and Thomas Dietterich. "Benchmarking Neural Network Robustness
  to Common Corruptions and Perturbations." ICLR 2019.
  https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.12261
  https://github.com/hendrycks/robustness

The full Apache License 2.0 text is in the LICENSE file next to this notice.

Modifications made for this project (Apache License 2.0, section 4(b)):

  * `skimage.filters.gaussian(..., multichannel=True)` replaced by
    `channel_axis=-1` (the old keyword was removed from scikit-image).
  * Global `np.random` state replaced by an explicit `numpy.random.Generator`
    argument so every corruption is deterministic for a given seed.
  * OpenCV (`cv2`) dependency removed: the disk kernel, defocus filter and
    RGB-to-gray conversion use scipy / numpy equivalents.
  * Removed NumPy 2 / SciPy incompatibilities (`np.float_`,
    `scipy.ndimage.interpolation`) and the `pkg_resources` import.
  * Grayscale-input branches were dropped (inputs are always RGB).
  * `frost` and `spatter` were not vendored (they need bundled texture images
    and OpenCV image-processing routines respectively).
  * Corruptions are called through `corrupt()` in `__init__.py`, which takes
    and returns `uint8` RGB arrays.
